WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.070
okay.

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.399
Time for audience questions for the week.

00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:03.399
First question.

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:07.970
Hey David, why are people calling what Donald
Trump did a quid pro quo instead of just calling

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.050
it bribery or extortion?

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.050
Very good question.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.130
And something I've been talking about

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.130
for a while.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.900
The the media cycles are basically referring
to it as a quid pro quo.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.551
And what I realized was the problem was that
there was a lot of debate over whether it

00:00:21.551 --> 00:00:26.279
was a quid pro quo without people knowing
what quid pro quo means, which of course I

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:31.999
think the, the gist of the Latin is a, you
scratch my back, I'll scratch yours.

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:34.710
Something for something else, something in
exchange for something else.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.649
This for that.

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:42.539
It is not in a literal Latin translation,
although I think that it's generally a accurate

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:46.870
when in reality if you don't actually understand
what that means, you might not understand

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:47.870
that.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:51.059
We're basically talking about actions by Donald
Trump that would be bribery or or extortion.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:53.109
So let's look at the definitions here.

00:00:53.109 --> 00:01:00.039
Quid pro quo defined in English would be a
favor or advantage granted or expected in

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:01.700
return for something.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:07.420
So it does describe what took place with,
we need you to do us a favor.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:13.070
The military aid smear investigations of Joe
Biden by Ukraine and the Ukrainian president

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:18.100
Zelenskyi quid pro quo is not an inaccurate
term, but a lot of people don't understand

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.189
it and it's probably not a strong enough term
bribery.

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:27.009
On the other hand, the giving or offering
of a bribe, which is a sum of money or other

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:35.380
inducement offered given, offered or given
to bribe someone, uh, seems to me a much more

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.210
precise and actually much more indicative
of the true sort of nature, scope and severity

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:44.500
of what has taken place to bribe is to persuade
someone to act in one's favor.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:52.439
For example, by smearing Joe Biden typically
illegally or at least dishonestly or immorally,

00:01:52.439 --> 00:01:56.219
you could argue via a gift of money or other
inducement.

00:01:56.219 --> 00:02:00.439
It is literally what is believed, what is
alleged to have taken place between Trump

00:02:00.439 --> 00:02:02.759
and the Ukrainian president.

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:07.840
There was the attempt by the Trump administration,
including on the July 25 phone call, but also

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.840
beyond it.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:15.980
What led up to it as we know in other conversations,
the idea was let's persuade Ukraine to publicly

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.830
announce an investigation of Joe Biden and
Hunter Biden for the purposes of hurting Joe

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:28.150
Biden's chances in 2020 to help Donald Trump
in exchange for a gift of money or inducement.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:31.660
In this case it was military aid money for
the country.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:40.400
Now what's interesting about that is the attempt
to persuade on that basis is the bribery regardless

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.020
of whether the bribe is accepted or ever actually
paid, and that is another reason why we really

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.890
should be calling it bribery instead of quid
pro quo.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:55.070
Quid pro quo accurately or inaccurately is
often interpreted as one thing for the other

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.580
and the things are exchanged.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:02.620
When you look at the different definition
of bribery and what a bribe is, the language

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:09.820
makes it much more clear that the attempt,
the persuasion attempt, the inducement, regardless

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:15.690
of whether it's accepted still counts as a,
as a bribe, as an attempted bribe, as bribery,

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.690
and that's really important.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:17.840
And then we also get to extortion.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:23.030
Now the definition of extortion is the practice
of obtaining something, especially money through

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.380
force or threats.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:33.350
So you can say that when you consider the
geopolitical imbalance of power between the

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:40.441
United States and Ukraine, you can reasonably
make the case that when a white house, when

00:03:40.441 --> 00:03:48.050
the Trump white house tries to obtain smears
on Joe Biden from Ukraine, they are using

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.810
force and threats.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.240
Is it physical force?

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.940
No, Trump is not saying he's going to show
up and punch president Zelenskyi.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:55.940
It's not that.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:01.230
But when you consider the power dynamic, we
could certainly argue that it is the use of

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.480
force to obtain something from Ukraine.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.590
And that in that sense it also qualifies as
extortion.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:11.000
So these are certainly more commonly known
and understood terms.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.850
I believe that they more precisely describe
what it is that took place.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:20.760
So I think that we can't not use the term
quid pro quo at all because it's still in

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.060
the conversation, but I'm going to make an
effort to say, um, what is being described

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.270
as a quid pro quo.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.870
It's actually a bribery and even extortion.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:32.290
I think I'm going to start making that point
every time and I appreciate you bringing it

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:32.311
up to me

